<h1>RoboSweeper — Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="muted">Last updated: October 26, 2026</p>

<h2>Who we are</h2>
<p>RoboSweeper (Android app <code>com.usefulappz.robosweeper</code>) is developed by Usefulappz™ (Mike Kelley). Contact: <a href="mailto:mikekelleyii.mk2@gmail.com">mikekelleyii.mk2@gmail.com</a></p>

<h2>The short version</h2>
<p>RoboSweeper displays the latest sweep report for the developer's own websites and apps — which revenue placements are open, which are missing, and which balances are being watched. The report is about <strong>our own properties, not about you</strong>. The app collects <strong>no personal data</strong>: no accounts, no analytics, no ads SDK, no tracking, and nothing is sold.</p>

<h2>How the app works</h2>
<ul>
  <li>The sweep itself runs on <strong>our server</strong> against our own site and affiliate placements. The app fetches the finished report — counts and placement states — from our server and displays it. That fetch carries none of your information.</li>
  <li>The app includes a <strong>root check</strong>: it detects whether the device it is running on is rooted and simply shows that result on screen. Rooted devices are welcome — the check never blocks, limits, or changes anything. It runs entirely on the device, and its result is not transmitted anywhere.</li>
</ul>

<h2>What the app stores</h2>
<p>Nothing about you. The report it displays is stored on our server and concerns our own websites and affiliate placements only.</p>

<h2>Permissions, and why</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Internet</strong> — used only to fetch the latest sweep report from our server, as described above.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Ads</h2>
<p>RoboSweeper contains <strong>no ads and no advertising SDK</strong>.</p>

<h2>Children</h2>
<p>RoboSweeper is a business tool. It is not directed at children under 13, and it collects no data from anyone.</p>

<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>If this policy changes, the new version will be posted at this URL with a new "last updated" date.</p>

